tel 1.0 specification.tel/tels:1.0.0
name tool

# The tool descriptor schema (builds.md §14.3): the document a tool's `descriptor`
# extracts to at publish (`tool.tel` in a lira-tool release's tree), and equally the
# registry entry shape for built-in tools (universes.md §6). Publishable as a tels/1
# module. The descriptor is the carrier-neutral information model: a WIT-hosted tool
# and a Scala-trait tool are the same kind of thing exactly when they extract
# identical descriptors.
#
# Atomization (the tool discipline, to be specified): one rigid atom per edge — the
# value covering its parameter, roles, forms, disciplines and component names — and
# one per setting with its classification; so dropping an edge or reclassifying a
# setting is graded. Naming: edges are addressed as <tool>/<edge-name>, the name
# defaulting to the output form.
#
# Parameterized edges: an edge may declare a parameter (triple, platform), bound at
# invocation and referenced in form names as an angle-bracket placeholder —
# `native-exe/<triple>` — unified along the hyperpath (builds.md §15.2): demanded at
# the outermost artifact, propagated backward to every parameterized edge en route.

scalar Form
  description  A registered form name (builds.md §14.1), possibly with a <parameter> placeholder
  validate     form

scalar DisciplineId
  description  A discipline identifier, e.g. tasty/1 (spec §11.1)
  validate     discipline-id

scalar Effect
  description  output — the setting affects output bytes and belongs in manifests; nothing — side-effect only, never recorded
  validate     effect

record Input
  description  A source-side form the edge consumes

  field form Form
  field optional Flag optional

# Settings here are SPECIFICATIONS (key + classification), not values: values are
# configured in build.tel and recorded, where output-affecting, in manifests via the
# section-scoped Tool records.
record Setting
  description  One setting specification, `set <key>` with its effect

  field key Identifier
  field affects Effect

record Component
  description  A separately-versioned constituent of the edge, named; versions are chosen in build.tel and locked

  field name Identifier

# Roles per builds.md §14.2: input is consumed (an egress's buildpath is input);
# context is read but not consumed (a compiler's dependency cells), with `employs`
# naming the disciplines read from context carriers and `emits` the carriers
# produced into the output.
record Edge
  description  One invocation kind, named by its output form unless stated

  field output Form
  field name Identifier optional
  field parameter Identifier optional
  field input Input optional repeatable
  field context Form optional repeatable
  field employs DisciplineId optional repeatable
  field emits DisciplineId optional repeatable
  field component Component optional repeatable
  field set Setting optional repeatable

document
  field name Identifier
  field edge Edge optional repeatable
  field set Setting optional repeatable  # tool-level: applies to every edge
